Main code complete. Now tests. Test setup:

- src/test/resources/application.yaml: H2 test db `jdbc:h2:mem:deicing-test;MODE=MySQL;DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1`, sql init always.
- MutableClock test clock: a @TestConfiguration that provides a primary Clock bean. But TimeConfig also defines a Clock bean — need @Primary on test clock.
- Test classes:
  1. DeicingFlowTest — main flow: 10:00 complete fluid A, 10:19 confirm OK, 10:20 rejected + reapply. Plus overlap 409, cancel rules, idempotency.
  2. ConcurrencyTest — concurrent overlapping apply (exactly one success), complete vs cancel race.
  3. QueryTest — timeline & clearances.

Cleanup: @BeforeEach delete from all tables (order matters due to FK): takeoff_rejection, takeoff_clearance, deicing_completion, deicing_slot. Keep airport/vehicle/flight seed data. Use fixed vehicle IDs — data.sql inserts with auto-increment; IDs will be 1.. for airport, vehicles 1,2, flights 1,2,3 since fresh DB. But DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1 shared across test classes in same JVM — cleanup only deletes slot/completion/clearance/rejection tables, so vehicle IDs stay 1,2 and flights 1,2,3. Good.

MutableClock: set Instant, instant() returns it. Test config:

```java
@TestConfiguration
static class TestClockConfig {
    @Bean @Primary MutableClock mutableClock() { return new MutableClock(Instant.parse("2026-01-01T09:00:00Z")); }
}
```

MutableClock extends Clock with settable instant, UTC zone.

Note: completeSlot uses clock for completedAt; confirmTakeoff uses clock for now. So scenario: apply slot, set clock 10:00, complete with A → deadline 10:20. Set clock 10:19 → confirm OK. New flight/slot: complete at 10:00, set clock 10:20 → confirm → 409 + rejection recorded. Then reapply new slot for same flight (overdue flight can re-apply) → success.

Concurrency test: 8 threads apply overlapping slots same vehicle, distinct requestIds, count successes == 1. Complete vs cancel race: apply slot, two threads (complete, cancel) with latch, assert exactly one success and final state consistent. H2 FOR UPDATE row lock: lockVehicle does SELECT ... FOR UPDATE — in H2 this locks the row; concurrent transactions on same vehicle row will serialize. MVCC default in H2 2.x — SELECT FOR UPDATE locks. Should work.

One concern: H2 in MySQL mode, `SELECT id FROM deicing_vehicle WHERE id = ? FOR UPDATE` — fine.

Transaction + concurrency: DeicingService.applySlot is @Transactional; threads each get own transaction via service proxy. Good.

For the complete/cancel race: both do conditional UPDATE ... WHERE status='SCHEDULED'. H2 default isolation READ_COMMITTED; the two updates serialize on row lock; one gets 1 row, other 0. Good.

Also idempotency test: same requestId same params replay returns same slot id; different params → 409. Takeoff confirm replay: same requestId → same clearance, only one clearance row; different requestId after clearance exists → completion_id unique → 409.

Wait: in confirmTakeoff, second confirm with different requestId: existing by requestId not found, latest completion found, now before deadline → tries insert → DuplicateKeyException on completion_id unique → 409 "该完成记录已用于放行". Good — "重复起飞确认不能生成第二次放行".

Edge: after rejection at 10:20, flight re-applies: new slot for same flight, different vehicle or non-overlapping time. Then complete with B, confirm → new clearance. Also test that old completion isn't reused: findLatestByFlightId returns latest by completed_at — after new completion, latest is new one. Good.

Also "作业未完成" confirm → 409 + rejection. Test: flight with slot SCHEDULED but not completed → confirm → 409.

Timeline query test: vehicle 1 has slots with completion → entries contain fluidType A, deadline. Clearances query returns record with fixed snapshot.

Now about the test for "10:19 可确认，10:20 被拒": use clock at exactly 10:20:00 → not before deadline → reject. And 10:19:59? Use 10:19 exactly. Also test boundary 10:20:00 rejected. Good.

Let me also double check data.sql idempotent inserts work in H2 MySQL mode: `INSERT ... SELECT ... WHERE NOT EXISTS` — H2 supports INSERT INTO ... SELECT with WHERE? `INSERT INTO t (a,b) SELECT 'x','y' WHERE NOT EXISTS (...)` — H2 supports SELECT without FROM? In H2, `SELECT 1 WHERE NOT EXISTS(...)` works? H2 supports `SELECT ... WHERE` without FROM? I believe H2 allows SELECT without FROM (yes, H2 supports it). VALUES might be safer: `INSERT INTO airport (code,name) SELECT 'ZTST','合成测试机场' WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM airport)` — H2 supports this syntax? H2 docs: INSERT supports "query" which can be a SELECT. SELECT without FROM is supported in H2. I'll verify at test run.

Actually since schema.sql uses CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS and data.sql runs each context start, the WHERE NOT EXISTS guards make it idempotent. Alternatively use MERGE. Let me keep and see test results.

Chinese in data.sql — file is UTF-8 no BOM, spring.sql.init.encoding=UTF-8 set. Good.

